cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite the following."
title: "quant-olmoe: BCJR-QAT and 2-bit trellis-coded quantization on consumer GPUs"
abstract: >-
  This repository hosts two related projects on extreme-low-bit LLM
  compression. (1) BCJR-QAT: a differentiable relaxation of
  trellis-coded weight quantization that replaces the non-differentiable
  Viterbi argmax with the BCJR forward-backward sum-product algorithm at
  temperature T, with a fused Triton kernel and end-to-end forward-KL
  distillation results on Llama-3.2-1B at 2 bpw. (2) qtip-olmoe (prior
  work, used as the QTIP-PTQ baseline): a 2-bit weight-only PTQ pipeline
  for OLMoE-1B-7B with per-expert routing-conditioned Hessian calibration,
  runnable end-to-end on a single consumer GPU.
